## 3. VRAM Safety & GPU Management
You are operating on a shared GPU environment (RTX 4070, 12GB VRAM) running Stable Diffusion Forge and local LLMs.
* **Coding Engine**: The local 14B model (`qwen2.5-coder-14b.gguf` on KoboldCPP port `5001`) fits entirely in VRAM and runs at 30-50 tokens/s. Use this for coding tasks. 30B+ models spill over into system memory, causing heavy CPU lag.
* **Connection**: Always interface with local LLMs using KoboldCPP at `http://localhost:5001/v1` or Ollama at `http://localhost:11434`.
* **VRAM Eviction**: When calling local LLMs, always ensure you release the model after generation. If calling Ollama, send the payload parameter `"keep_alive": "0s"` to prevent VRAM hostage locks.

